WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.640
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) The stars are gone.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.340
The planets have disappeared.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.980
There were barely enough of us left to give the end a

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:13.340
name.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.220
The Quiet Rapture.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.620
Supplies dwindle.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.340
Infrastructure crumbles.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.380
Too few to rebuild.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.460
Too many to feed.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.220
Humanity decays.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.740
But don't despair, my sons.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.620
I tell you now that there is more to these moons than

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.460
meets the eye.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.920
The consolidation.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.400
They hide their technology, their people.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.880
They won't tell you what they found, but I will.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.480
One moon stands apart from the rest.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:20.330
And in the darkness of that moon, an ocean of blood.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.840
Beginning the descent.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.960
Exploration of AT-5 underway.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.100
How's it looking down there, convict?

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.280
Ready to do some good for a change?

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:27.820
Yeah.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.040
Let's get this done.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:30.760
Roger that.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.940
Cruising depth in roughly two minutes.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:34.820
Stand by.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.520
I'm seeing some voltage irregularities on the instrument, so keep an eye

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.740
out for sparks or flames or anything like that.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:44.620
Flames?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.440
Why would there be flames?

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.580
I don't know.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.200
That's why I warned you.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.220
You did test this thing, right?

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.500
This is the test.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.260
But you're welded in as tight as we can make it in

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:58.840
that ship's tank.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.960
Just keep an eye on your depth while you're down there.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.100
The terrain can be unpredictable, so make sure you're not wandering down

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.180
too far into the red.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.520
It can take pressure, but there's a limit.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.420
I'm starting to feel it, that glass.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:14.980
All right.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.840
Closing porthole shielding.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.200
Hey, what is it exactly you want me to find?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.700
You haven't told me what it is.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.880
We don't know.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.920
You're the first one down.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.740
All we have are surface scans.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:26.840
That's why you're there.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.060
Well, one of the reasons.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.920
You know, we salvaged that glass from Filament Station.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.940
A lot of scratch on it.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:37.660
Right?

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:38.880
Pretty lucky.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.160
Funny how some things survive and others don't.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.480
Approaching maximum depth.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:48.020
30 seconds.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.940
Hey, um, hey, are you hearing this?

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:55.500
Hello?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:56.760
Hey.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.020
Uh, hey, you said not to go into the red.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.160
We're in the red.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.480
Ready to lose radio signal.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.920
Head to the coordinates, the map, and cap it, and as instructed,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.560
we'll consider your pay as served.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.300
Be careful.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.140
Love your own.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.160
No.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:14.300
Hey!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:15.220
Hey!

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.420
You can't be serious.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.280
You can't be serious.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.440
You can't be serious.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.870
Fuck me.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:18.880
One minute.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:20.560
Fifty.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.560
Camera.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.220
That's useful.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:34.620
Oxygen.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.120
Twenty-six.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.220
Way off.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.550
It's not even on the map.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:26.010
Maybe.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.020
Hey, what do I do if I find something not on the

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:40.320
map?

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.580
You're not just pretending you can't hear me, right?

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.820
Why is it so fucking hot down here?

00:13:44.370 --> 00:14:18.380
I'm here.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.410
Uh, dude, I, I, I don't know.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:25.230
Was that you?

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:29.750
What is it?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.950
You didn't tell me that there would be anything down here.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:33.510
Calm down.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.390
Just tell me there's a problem with the ship.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.850
Do you know if the ship is damaged before we send you

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.350
back down?

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.070
Back?

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:40.190
Back down?

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:40.990
Back down?

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:41.350
No.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.210
No fucking way!

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.410
I'm done.

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:47.230
I'm done.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.270
So just bring me back up and throw me in prison.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.470
I'm not doing this!

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:58.170
If they're damaged, tell me if there's a problem with the sub,

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.690
because if you fell, the hull could be punctured, which means a

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:04.930
leak, which means flooding, which means you die.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:20.380
Um, um, it seems fine.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:22.740
Good.

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:23.140
Good.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.900
I can't see much, but it seems like the hull is in

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.000
one piece, so we're going to check on your progress while we

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.500
wait for the ocean to settle back down.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.680
Hey, do you think we can get any pictures?

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.940
I mean, you could get a couple, maybe.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.300
Yeah, well, it might take a while to settle, so go ahead.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.120
Uh, settle?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.020
What does that mean?

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.520
Um, is that why everything was shaking?

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:46.720
Essentially, yeah.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.360
The bottom isn't exactly rock, just layers of congealed blood and gas

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:51.740
bubbles.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.760
That's why I said it wasn't stable.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.020
What?

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:56.640
You may want to see this.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.480
That's the most recent picture.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:15:59.800
Holy shit.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.900
Convicts, you're...

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.700
Did you find a skeleton?

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:04.520
Yeah.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:07.200
Yeah.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.380
This could just be rock skin.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.840
Can you get me a higher resolution?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.940
Look at this.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.280
Yes, I am.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:17.200
Convict, are you absolutely sure that it was a skeleton?

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:17.860
Yeah.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.160
I've seen a skeleton before.

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:22.460
How stupid do you think I am?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:26.910
We're pulling you up.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:27.770
Stand by.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:11.440
Huh?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:54.380
Hey, so, uh, so what's the deal?

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:55.040
Am I done?

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.240
How's your afternoon?

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:57.480
Any leaks?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:02.600
Uh, um, uh, yeah, I'm down a lot, but, yeah, maybe.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:03.780
There might be a leak.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.480
There was some blood dripping in, and then there's some kind of

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.760
liquid building up on the walls.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:09.900
I don't know what it was.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.260
It's just a condensation.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:13.020
I know a condensation.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.000
Look, it doesn't matter.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.280
You just warn the next person that goes down what I found.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.820
There's something alive down there.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.300
Hey, yeah, so I found something, right?

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:01.180
Something good?

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.060
We downloaded the picture.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.320
Sure looks like a skeleton to me.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:08.720
Come on, get me out of here.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.060
You can't.

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:12.380
Like I said, you're welded in.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.720
You take your time getting in.

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:17.880
Another slip might go somewhere that we can't get, so I'm going

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.220
to give you something to take a sample.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:21.600
Hey!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.160
You're not listening to me!

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:24.620
There's something else!

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.160
Okay, it's not like I don't want the deal, all right?

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:29.900
I want the deal.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.920
I want to make...

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:33.680
It's not worth it.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.120
It's not.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:37.940
It's not worth it for me.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.360
It's not worth it for you.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.740
Fawning over this skeleton, but you're not hearing me when I say

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.800
there's something else.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:46.760
Something alive.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:50.670
There might just be.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.340
Right up front.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:59.360
All you got to do is point it in the right direction.

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:02.420
Once it makes contact, it should be able to grab onto something

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.320
and hold on tight.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:05.780
So what am I supposed to do?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:06.540
Just ram it?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:08.260
Pretty much.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.220
You can't be serious.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:11.880
I am.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:14.580
You'll have to hit it hard, too.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:16.520
Hard enough to make sure that it catches.

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:18.700
You won't be able to see if it works, so no second

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:19.280
chances.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:22.440
Okay, so you don't just want me to ram it.

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:24.780
You want me to ram it at full speed?

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:26.180
Why play games?

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:27.980
Why go through all this trouble?

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.780
If you want me dead so bad, why don't you just do

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.200
it yourself?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.040
This is the best we have.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.120
This is bigger than any of us, so just do your job.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.300
My job?

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.040
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.040
The handcuffs must have confused me.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.700
I didn't realize this was voluntary!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.080
Hey!

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.080
Don't walk away!

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:57.220
If this don't bond you, why aren't you going down there?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.040
Hey!

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:02.700
Go down, come back, and then I'm free!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.160
That was the deal!

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.760
How many times are you going to use me before you let

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:08.600
me go?

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:25.320
Oh, good.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.020
You can hear me.

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:30.160
Now get someone else for your suicide mission, because I'm not going

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:33.180
to let this radiation you sent over here fuck!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:38.050
It's not a normal camera.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.810
You can't see through blood, so you need x-rays to get

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:42.250
through.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.310
I didn't know that.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.170
Okay, it's on.

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:47.910
Hey, let me show you.

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:49.130
I didn't know that.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:57.600
No, wait.

00:21:57.760 --> 00:22:00.260
Look, I'm sorry, but maybe if you had talked to me, this

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:00.980
wouldn't have happened!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:12.120
I'm just going to sit here.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.240
Come on, guy, back together.

00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:56.960
Don't be too upset.

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.420
Kind of a fair play after what you did.

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:03.540
Oh, shit, are you still alive?

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.600
Fuck off.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.440
Ah, there you are.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.620
All right, beginning the descent.

00:23:17.150 --> 00:23:21.010
Uh, hey, you, uh, you gotta close the portal shield, man.

00:23:22.890 --> 00:23:23.430
Hello?

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.170
Convict, this is Sirius.

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:28.590
Close the shield.

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:29.510
Who is this?

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:31.590
Where's the other one?

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.560
The other one, you're talking about Jack, the guy you irradiated?

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:38.910
Well, Captain's taking him to medical, so I'm in charge now.

00:23:39.190 --> 00:23:42.630
And my first order is close the fucking shield.

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:45.570
Why can't you do it?

00:23:45.970 --> 00:23:49.030
It's not responsible, which is why we have you.

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:50.170
Is it closed?

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:51.450
Yes, it's closed.

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:54.770
Now, we're going to give you about 30 minutes to go get

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:56.850
that sample before we pull you back up.

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:00.690
Don't worry, I know ramming it sounds scary, but the salvage clods

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:03.150
and most of the impact of those welds aren't going anywhere.

00:24:03.350 --> 00:24:05.170
This Jack is good at his job.

00:24:05.370 --> 00:24:09.170
Or, let me repeat, well, he was good at his job.

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:11.830
You didn't think it was important to tell me that your camera

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:12.950
was a radiation gun?

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:13.630
No, I wouldn't.

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:16.430
That shouldn't have happened at all.

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:20.310
Well, the camera's wired into the black box, but I must have

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:21.890
wired it into the back of that.

00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:23.550
We were in a rush.

00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:24.330
Right.

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:27.250
Things are somehow faster when I don't know what I'm doing.

00:24:27.550 --> 00:24:29.690
You know, honestly, if I were in charge, you would know more.

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.030
I'd actually give us the results on a nod.

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:33.530
I'm just a cognitive machine.

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:37.250
But, you know, this is bigger than us.

00:24:38.110 --> 00:24:38.990
So I've heard.

00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:43.550
Well, man, can we just agree this is important?

00:24:43.550 --> 00:24:46.890
The filament station was a bad loss, but imagine if we could

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:48.130
actually rebuild it.

00:24:48.670 --> 00:24:49.870
Even you could be a part of that.

00:24:50.410 --> 00:24:51.250
I read your report.

00:24:51.330 --> 00:24:51.990
You surrendered.

00:24:52.390 --> 00:24:55.190
Still fooling by Eden's bullshit?

00:24:55.650 --> 00:24:58.050
All their talk about the last tree.

00:24:58.570 --> 00:24:59.810
It's not about the tree.

00:25:00.590 --> 00:25:00.750
Right.

00:25:01.230 --> 00:25:02.510
But Eden gave me a tattoo.

00:25:03.190 --> 00:25:05.190
The COI made me burn it off.

00:25:06.050 --> 00:25:07.590
I didn't choose either of them.

00:25:08.610 --> 00:25:09.830
I still get a scar.

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:12.110
Since the Quiet Rapture.

00:25:12.970 --> 00:25:14.630
None of us get a choice.

00:25:14.770 --> 00:25:15.630
Hey, look at that.

00:25:16.150 --> 00:25:17.430
There's at least something we can agree on.

00:25:18.010 --> 00:25:20.590
To be honest with you, Captain's had a consolidated stick up her

00:25:20.590 --> 00:25:21.710
ass in the Quiet Rapture.

00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:24.370
But, uh, she cares about her crew.

00:25:25.210 --> 00:25:26.950
Some more than others, but, you know.

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:28.070
Yeah, right.

00:25:29.190 --> 00:25:31.490
Can you at least tell me if this thing is blasting me

00:25:31.490 --> 00:25:31.970
with radiation?

00:25:32.350 --> 00:25:33.990
No, the hull's fucked up.

00:25:44.990 --> 00:25:46.030
Food, air.

00:25:46.430 --> 00:25:46.790
We need this.

00:25:46.790 --> 00:25:48.250
It's not just the COI.

00:25:48.310 --> 00:25:48.950
All of us.

00:25:48.950 --> 00:25:50.030
We need this.

00:25:51.830 --> 00:25:52.340
Shit.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:04.300
This is

00:26:07.980 --> 00:26:21.160
not

00:28:57.770 --> 00:28:58.670
an expedition.

00:29:00.890 --> 00:29:02.270
It's an execution.

00:29:04.330 --> 00:29:08.950
When they put you in here, they don't want you to return.

00:29:10.130 --> 00:29:14.230
And even if you do, and even if they keep their promises,

00:29:15.330 --> 00:29:17.650
what freedom waits for you?

00:29:19.130 --> 00:29:23.350
A few dying ships and a sea of dead stars.

00:29:24.610 --> 00:29:29.070
If there is still hope, it lies beyond the veil.

00:29:30.250 --> 00:29:35.890
Hope in this void is as illusionary as the starlight.

00:29:37.490 --> 00:29:41.990
I will choose to breathe my last here.

00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:45.410
At the bottom of an ocean.

00:29:47.570 --> 00:29:48.210
Unseen.

00:29:50.370 --> 00:29:50.910
Unheard.

00:29:53.190 --> 00:29:54.370
Uncontrolled.